#: metadata.json->name
msgid "T2 Fan (AUTO / MAX)"
msgstr ""

#: metadata.json->description
msgid "Fan control for Intel Macs with the Apple T2 chip running Linux (t2fanrd service): one click toggles AUTO and MAX, with Strong, Medium and Quiet AUTO profiles and live CPU temperature and fan RPM."
msgstr ""

#: metadata.json->comments
msgid "Left click: AUTO ↔ MAX.\nRight click: AUTO profile, live readings and options.\n\nAUTO profiles:\n  Strong: 40–60 °C, logarithmic curve\n  Medium: 50–75 °C, linear curve\n  Quiet: 60–85 °C, exponential curve\n\nRequires t2fanrd (t2linux project) and Cinnamon.\nTested on a Mac mini 2018 (Macmini8,1) with Cinnamon 6.6.\n\nAuthor: pepsimo — https://www.pepsimo.es\nCo-author: Claude Opus 5.5 (Anthropic)\nSource code and documentation: https://github.com/pepsimo/t2fan-control\nLicense: GPL-3.0-or-later. No warranty of any kind."
msgstr ""

